<header class="page-hero">
  <h1>Two projects for the cockpit and the ground</h1>
  <p class="page-hero-subtitle">We&rsquo;re designing skyBlip Panel and the skyPost stations. They aren&rsquo;t available to buy.</p>
</header>

<section id="on-board" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">In the cockpit: show traffic on the aircraft&rsquo;s display</h2>
  <p>skyBlip Panel will mount behind the instrument panel. It will run on aircraft power and have no screen of its own. It will transmit your position and receive traffic in ADS-L, the European standard for sharing position by radio. Traffic will appear on a cockpit display such as a Garmin G3X or Dynon SkyView. Panel will send traffic over a serial cable, Bluetooth or Wi-Fi.</p>
  <p>Panel will use a LilyGO T-Beam Supreme board and a MAX3232 RS-232 adapter.</p>
  <figure class="shot shot--photo">
    <%= pages_image_tag "skyblip-panel-board.avif", alt: "The skyBlip Panel board in its case, with its antenna." %>
  </figure>
</section>

<section id="on-the-ground" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">On the ground: relay traffic and weather around an airfield</h2>
  <p>A skyPost station will receive ADS-B, the position data that equipped aircraft transmit by radio. It will add traffic from the Open Glider Network (OGN) and airfield weather: the altimeter setting (QNH), the latest observation (METAR) and the forecast (TAF). It will relay these over ADS-L to skyBlip Go devices in range.</p>
  <h3 id="helio">skyPost Helio</h3>
  <p>Helio will mount on a mast in a weatherproof case. It will run on solar power and receive ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM, a position-sharing system widely used in gliding. It will use a LilyGO T-Beam Supreme board, an Ebyte E80-900MBL receiver and a LilyGO T-Solar kit.</p>
  <h3 id="bridge">skyPost Bridge</h3>
  <p>Bridge will work alongside existing OGN, PiAware or adsb.lol stations. It will relay the traffic they already receive in ADS-L without changing their data feeds. It will use a LilyGO T-Beam Supreme board.</p>
